{
  "contract": "pcc.evidence.input-commitment.v1",
  "description": "Per-job v1: exact raw SHA-256 bytes bridge method_loaded.payload.inputHash to the authenticated FUNDED SubjectBlockFields.recipeRef (accepted-policy.ts:494), never a CSD binding's params.recipeRef (process.batch_record's paramsSchema) (#8812/#8815). recipeRef must be in spec-canonical lowercase, the only form computeSubjectBlockHash admits. A consumer whose subject-block authentication accepts other spellings (the oracle's ethers ABI coder does) lowercases the AUTHENTICATED value once, then calls these functions. The inputHash side is never normalized. Zero recipeRef means no commitment.",
